{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789944936,"nonce":"IhGt5/IoihzGWK6CM3e8fb+/cW8=","title":"A `T` handed to a Dynamic slot was never boxed; Std.isOfType(v, Int) tested against type id 0","message":"Two defects, found with a self-checking generic-class probe.\n\n1. `maybe_box_value_inner` skipped `TypeKind::TypeParameter` (\"unsupported\n   type\"), so `function dyn():Dynamic return v` with `v:T` returned the raw\n   i64 slot and the caller read the bits as a box (`7 \u003cunknown type\u003e\n   4612811918334230528`). `box_value_for_dynamic` (Type.typeof's path) fell\n   to the erased I64 and boxed every T as Int (`typeof` gave TInt for a\n   Float/String/Bool T). Both now go through `haxe_box_typed_ptr` with a\n   `type_param_tag_fixups` placeholder the monomorphizer fills from the\n   instance's binding — the mechanism the Optional-inner-T path already used.\n   The runtime's Reference arm tags a class instance from its header, so\n   `Std.string` reaches the class's toString. An Array or anonymous `T` has\n   no header and still boxes untyped (prints `void`) — the MIR type argument\n   is `Ptr(Void)` for both, so the tag cannot tell them apart at compile time.\n   An enum `T` (IrType I64) boxes as Int; also open.\n\n2. `Std.isOfType(v, Int)` desugars to TypeCheck with `expected` = the type of\n   the `Int` expression, which is the StdTypes `abstract Int`, not\n   `TypeKind::Int` (`Float`/`Bool` likewise; `String` is the String class).\n   `runtime_type_id` had no Abstract arm and answered 0, so every\n   `Std.isOfType(dynamicValue, Int|Float|Bool)` was false, and every static\n   `Std.isOfType(7, String)` fell to the permissive `true`. `canonical_type_ref`\n   maps those four names back to the primitive kinds before matching.\n   `Std.isOfType(7, Float)` is true (Haxe: an Int is a Float) in both the\n   static arm and `haxe_std_is`.\n\nTwo guards the first gate demanded:\n\n- A `T` the current MIR function does not declare (a leaked monomorph such as\n  `Type.createInstance`'s T in a non-generic caller) has nothing to fill its\n  tag, so it keeps the old path: raw for boxing, `true` for isOfType\n  (Issue8717 went LOST without this).\n- A `T` argument into a GENERIC callee's Dynamic formal stays raw. An\n  unannotated parameter of a generic function decays to Dynamic while the\n  body reads the slot as the `T` it is (`ArraySort.upper(a, cmp, from, to,\n  val)`, `TreeNode.new(l, k, v, r)`): boxing there put a box in the key slot\n  and `Reflect.compare` read it as the key (test_balancedtree_crossmodule_mono\n  SIGSEGV at fault 0x5). The unannotated-parameter inference also now reads\n  bare `field = param` stores, not only `this.field = param`, which types\n  TreeNode's constructor properly.\n\nStill wrong: `Std.isOfType(([1]:Dynamic), Array)` is false (the typed cast\nof an array literal does not box as an array); `Std.isOfType(x, Dynamic)`;\nan Array/anonymous/enum `T` into Dynamic (see above). Issue6722\n(ArraySort.sort through a Dynamic-typed `cmp` field) is BISTABLE on HEAD\nalready -- [0,3,1] / SIGSEGV / hang across runs -- and is a separate issue.\n\nFixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/TypeParamToDynamic.hx","files":null}]}